  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load the knowledge files, read the relevant files listed above, declare rigor and model tier per task-execute Step 0.5.</step>
    <step order="1">Read the task-033 message filter, the grant row shape (src/solutions/SpaarkeCore/entities/sprk_externalrecordaccess/entity-schema.md) and the distributed-cache pattern.</step>
    <step order="2">Create ExternalNotificationFeedEndpoints.cs (Map method called from ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs in the external group).</step>
    <step order="3">Build the feed from grants + messages with the bounds above; compute unreadCount from the last-seen marker.</step>
    <step order="4">POST /notifications/seen writes the marker.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: new grant appears; new message on an accessible record appears; caller's own message does not; internal-only message never appears for a contact; record outside the set never appears; unreadCount drops to 0 after /seen; items older than 30 days excluded; cache miss → all items unread.</step>
    <step order="6">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` (0 errors) and `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` (all pass); measure publish size per .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md and record it in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` and this POML's &lt;status&gt; to completed; run `pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1`.</step>
    <step order="8">Record deviations, decisions and measurements in projects/spaarke-SPA-external-access-platform-r3/notes/task-037-notes.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If grants for systemuser callers are not represented in sprk_externalrecordaccess (so licensed staff would see only messages), record it in notes/decisions.md and continue — do not invent a grant source.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No feed endpoint exists; appnotification (Dataverse) targets systemusers only, so it cannot serve contacts.</existing>
    <extension>No: there is no external notification surface to extend; the feed reuses the message read rules (033) and the existing grant rows.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Users have no in-portal notice of new access or messages (G3, owner 2026-08-12).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalNotificationFeedEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalNotificationFeedTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A grant to the caller within 30 days appears in the feed with its record type, id and title.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A message by someone else on an accessible record within 30 days appears; the caller's own messages do not.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An internal-only message never appears for a contact caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A record outside the caller's accessible set never appears, even if a grant row or message exists.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">unreadCount counts items newer than last-seen; after POST /seen it is 0 until a newer item arrives.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Items older than 30 days are excluded and at most 100 items are returned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build is green; all unit tests pass; publish size is recorded and at or under 60 MB with no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the negative and edge cases named in these criteria. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-08. Client: task 055.</notes>

